<LegalLayout title="Terms of Service" description="Terms for using the live Brev Cloud service and the Brev self-hosted software.">
<h2>1. What Brev is</h2>
  <h3>Brev Cloud</h3>
  <p>Brev Cloud is the live managed link service at <a href="https://brevl.ink">brevl.ink</a>. It is currently free of charge. There are no active paid plans or payment flows. Custom domains are available at no extra cost.</p>
  <h3>Brev self-hosted</h3>
  <p>The software is distributed under the <a href="https://github.com/brevlink/brev/blob/main/LICENSE">MIT licence</a>. Each operator is responsible for their installation, infrastructure, users, data, logs, updates and compliance. Brand use is governed by <a href="https://github.com/brevlink/brev/blob/main/TRADEMARK.md">TRADEMARK.md</a>.</p>

  <h2>2. Accounts</h2>
  <p>Register with an email address and password. Provide accurate account data. Keep your password and API keys secure and notify us of unauthorised access at <a href="mailto:abuse@brevl.ink">abuse@brevl.ink</a>.</p>
  <p>Use one account per person. Do not share account access without authorisation. To share a domain, invite a member instead. Email verification is required before you can use links, domains or API keys.</p>
  <p>You may use Brev Cloud if you meet the minimum age for consenting to online services in your country, which is 14 in Italy. Otherwise, you may use it only with a parent or guardian.</p>

  <h2>3. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>You must not use Brev for:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Unlawful activity, phishing, malware or spam.</li>
    <li>Harmful or dangerous content, infringement of rights or harassment.</li>
    <li>Evading blocks or impersonating Brev or another person or organisation.</li>
    <li>Using links to conceal abuse.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Report abuse to <a href="mailto:abuse@brevl.ink">abuse@brevl.ink</a> or through <a href="https://brevl.ink/app/report">Report a link</a>. Report security issues through <a href="https://github.com/brevlink/brev/security/advisories/new">GitHub Security Advisories</a>. We may disable links, domains or accounts that breach these rules.</p>

  <h2>4. Your content and your domains</h2>
  <p>You retain the rights to your content and URLs. You authorise Brev to store destination URLs, resolve redirects and count clicks to provide the service.</p>
  <p>You must have the right to use any domain you add. The DNS verification token proves control of the domain. Do not share it with members.</p>

  <h2>5. Shared domains</h2>
  <p>The domain owner invites members by email address and can view and remove them. Members can publish links on the shared domain and can leave it.</p>

  <h2>6. Availability and changes</h2>
  <p>The service is provided as is, without a service level agreement or guarantees beyond those required by law. We may change or discontinue features.</p>
  <p>We may suspend an account for security, abuse or a breach of these terms. You can delete your account at any time from the account panel.</p>

  <h2>7. Liability</h2>
  <p>Any limitation of liability applies only to the extent permitted by law. Nothing in these terms excludes liability that cannot lawfully be excluded, including for intentional misconduct, gross negligence, personal injury or consumer rights.</p>
  <p>Consumers retain the mandatory protections of their country of residence.</p>

  <h2>8. Payments</h2>
  <p>No payments are active today. Stripe is not configured. If a paid plan is introduced, we will publish the price, currency, taxes, charge timing, receipt details and refund policy before any charge. These terms will be updated beforehand.</p>

  <h2>9. Governing law and jurisdiction</h2>
  <p>Italian law applies. Consumers retain the mandatory protections of their country of residence. For consumers, the competent court is that of their place of residence or domicile. In other cases, Italian courts have jurisdiction.</p>

  <h2>10. Changes and contacts</h2>
  <p>These documents are in English. The version and last updated date appear above. Changes update that version and date. Material changes will be published on the website and communicated to registered users.</p>
  <p>For privacy matters, contact <a href="mailto:privacy@brevl.ink">privacy@brevl.ink</a>. For abuse reports, contact <a href="mailto:abuse@brevl.ink">abuse@brevl.ink</a>.</p>
</LegalLayout>
